# 0. GOLDEN CODE PATTERNS(STRICTLY ENFORCE THESE)

### Pattern A: Next.js 15 Async Page Props(Server Components ONLY)
    ** Rule:** In Next.js 15, `params` and `searchParams` are Promises.You MUST await them in Server Components before usage.

```typescript
interface PageProps {
  params: Promise<{ id: string }>;
  searchParams: Promise<{ [key: string]: string | string[] | undefined }>;
}

export default async function Page(props: PageProps) {
  // 1. Await props strictly before usage
  const params = await props.params;
  const searchParams = await props.searchParams;
  
  // 2. UI: Simplified Chinese
  return <div className="p-4">设备ID: {params.id}</div>;
}
Pattern B: The "Strict-Mode Safe" MQTT Hook
Rule: Handle React 18/19 Strict Mode lifecycle (Mount -> Unmount -> Mount). Ensure connection idempotency and stable Client IDs.

TypeScript
// imports: import mqtt, { MqttClient } from 'mqtt';
const clientRef = useRef<MqttClient | null>(null);

useEffect(() => {
  // 1. Idempotency Check: If ref exists, we are already connected/connecting.
  if (clientRef.current) return; 

  // 2. Init with stable ID to prevent connection thrashing
  const clientId = `web_${ Date.now() }_${ Math.random().toString(16).slice(2, 6) } `;
  const client = mqtt.connect(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_MQTT_URL!, {
    clientId, 
    keepalive: 60,
    clean: true, 
  });
  clientRef.current = client;

  // 3. Events
  client.on('connect', () => {
    console.log('MQTT Connected');
    toast.success('设备已连接');
  });
  
  // 4. Cleanup: Explicitly end session on unmount to prevent zombie connections
  return () => {
    if (clientRef.current) {
      console.log('Cleanly ending MQTT session...');
      clientRef.current.end(true); 
      clientRef.current = null;
    }
  };
}, []);
Pattern C: Safe Server Actions (Strict Typing)
Rule: NEVER use any. Define ActionState with strict generics <T> or unknown. Use useActionState compatible patterns.

TypeScript
'use server';

import { z } from 'zod';

// 1. Define Strict Interface WITHOUT any
export type ActionState<T = unknown> = {
  success: boolean;
  message: string;
  errors?: Record<string, string[]>;
  payload?: T;
};

const schema = z.object({
  deviceId: z.string().min(1, "设备ID不能为空"),
  command: z.enum(['OPEN', 'CLOSE']),
});

// 2. Strictly Typed Function Signature
export async function sendCommandAction(prevState: ActionState, formData: FormData): Promise<ActionState> {
  const rawData = Object.fromEntries(formData);
  const parsed = schema.safeParse(rawData);
  
  if (!parsed.success) {
    return { 
      success: false, 
      message: '参数校验失败', 
      errors: parsed.error.flatten().fieldErrors 
    };
  }

  try {
    // Business Logic...
    return { success: true, message: '指令发送成功' };
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
    return { success: false, message: '服务器内部错误' };
  }
}
Rule: Use Zustand's granular selectors to ensure high-frequency IoT updates (coordinates, battery) only re-render specific "Leaf Components", not the entire map or dashboard.

TypeScript
// Pattern D: High-Performance Reactive Updates
// Rule: Use granular selectors and shallow to minimize re-renders for IoT streams.

import { useIoTStore } from '@/store/useIoTStore';
import { useShallow } from 'zustand/react/shallow';

export function MapMarker() {
  // 1. Granular Selector: This component ONLY re-renders when coordinates change
  const coords = useIoTStore(
    useShallow((state) => state.droneCoords)
  );

  return (
    <>
      {/* 2. Map Marker (Auto-syncs with React state) */}
      <AMapMarker position={[coords.lng, coords.lat]} />

      {/* 3. Floating Text (Easy to maintain, stays in sync) */}
      <div className="absolute top-4 left-4 p-2 bg-white shadow">
        当前位置: {coords.lng.toFixed(4)}, {coords.lat.toFixed(4)}
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
  // 3. Cleanup subscription
  return unsub;
}, []); // Dependency Array MUST be empty
CRITICAL ENGINEERING GUIDELINES
Next.js 15 Compatibility & Data Fetching

Async Components: Treat params, searchParams, headers(), cookies() as Promises in Server Components.

Client Components: Use useParams() and useSearchParams() hooks.

Caching: Explicitly use revalidatePath after Server Actions.

Environment & Architecture

Isolation: lib/env/server.ts MUST contain import 'server-only'.

Client Boundary: Use 'use client' ONLY at the leaf nodes (interactive components). Keep layout and data-fetching at the Server Component level.

Docker Friendly: Do not use Vercel-specific features (Edge Config, ImageResponse) as we deploy on standalone Docker.

UI/UX Standards

Language: ALL user-facing strings (Button labels, Placeholders, Toasts, Error messages) MUST be Simplified Chinese.

Styling: Use Tailwind CSS exclusively. Group utility classes logically.

Components: Use shadcn/ui. Import icons from lucide-react.

Responsive: Mobile-First approach.

Cursor Workflow

Analyze: Determine if the request requires a Client Component (Interactive) or Server Component (Data Fetching).

Match: Identify which "Golden Pattern" applies (MQTT, AMap, or Action).

Execute: Generate code using the pattern.

Localize: Verify all UI text is Chinese.

Audit: Check for forbidden synchronous access to params. Check that AMap updates are NOT causing re-renders.